<%# 002 FR-003/FR-004: the saved floor and locker number, shown once a floor exists.
    Reads the saved values rather than the attributes, so a rejected edit shows
    the error next to what is still on file instead of next to itself.

    009 FR-007: the way in to editing is the pencil in the corner. The caller
    passes editable: false while a swap proposal holds these values, where
    005's explanation takes the control's place.

    022: plain content on the homepage rather than a card — this partial's
    only call site is home/index.html.erb, so the card classes are dropped
    here directly instead of behind a flag with a single value everywhere it
    would be checked (research.md §3). "Your locker search" above it keeps
    its own card unchanged. %>
<div id="locker-profile" class="locker-profile">
  <div class="stack-tight">
    <h2 class="card-title"><%= t(".title") %></h2>

    <%# 032 FR-001, research.md R2: read the same way `current_user.saved_floor`/
        `saved_locker_number` below — directly through current_user, not an
        ivar — since this partial has two renderers (HomeController and
        LockerProfilesController on a rejected edit), per this file's own note
        at the top. %>
    <% zone_name = LockerMapEntry.zone_name_for(current_user.saved_floor, current_user.saved_locker_number) %>
    <%# detail-grid--zone: opt-in third grid column (application.css), only
        while this card actually has a zone field to put in it — a card with
        just Floor and Locker number keeps the plain 2-column layout every
        other .detail-grid on the site already has. %>
    <dl class="detail-grid <%= "detail-grid--zone" if zone_name %>">
      <div>
        <dt class="detail-term"><%= t(".floor") %></dt>
        <dd id="locker-profile-floor" class="detail-value"><%= current_user.saved_floor %></dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <dt class="detail-term"><%= t(".locker_number") %></dt>
        <%# FR-004: having no locker is an ordinary state, so it is styled as plain
            content rather than as a warning or an error. %>
        <dd id="locker-profile-locker-number" class="detail-value <%= "detail-value-empty" if current_user.saved_locker_number.blank? %>">
          <%= current_user.saved_locker_number.presence || t(".no_locker_assigned") %>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <%# A third field of this same grid, not the shared/_zone_label
          partial's inline "Zone: X" sentence: on the homepage the zone is
          uniform with Floor and Locker number — same term/value markup, same
          row at desktop, no colon, its own bold label at every width (French
          follow-up request, 2026-09-26). Omitted entirely when absent
          (FR-005), the same as it always was — an empty grid cell is not
          shown. %>
      <% if zone_name %>
        <div>
          <dt class="detail-term"><%= t("shared.zone_label") %></dt>
          <dd id="locker-profile-zone" class="detail-value"><%= zone_name %></dd>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <% if local_assigns.fetch(:editable, true) %>
    <%# 002 FR-009: editing is deliberate, so the form sits behind this control. A
        rejected submission reopens it, otherwise the error would have nowhere to
        show. <details> gives the disclosure keyboard and screen reader support
        without any JavaScript of its own, which is why 009 changes what the
        control looks like and not what it is.

        009 FR-009: the label the summary used to carry as text is now on
        aria-label, so the icon still says what it does to a screen reader. The
        drawing itself is hidden from the accessibility tree — it would otherwise
        be read out a second time, under whatever name the reader invents for
        it. %>
    <details class="locker-profile-editor" <%= "open" if current_user.errors.any? %>>
      <summary class="locker-profile-editor-summary" aria-label="<%= t(".edit_locker_details") %>">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
             aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M4 20h4L19.5 8.5a2.83 2.83 0 0 0-4-4L4 16v4Z"/>
          <path d="m14.5 5.5 4 4"/>
        </svg>
      </summary>

      <div class="locker-profile-editor-body">
        <%= render "home/locker_profile_form" %>
      </div>
    </details>
  <% end %>
</div>
